    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97115" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρᾰτηγ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>office of general, command</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				678
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				704
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				100
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				22
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλύειν τινὰ τῆς
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.94
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάσσων Ἑλλάδος
			στρατηγίας</span> being chief general of Greece, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυραννίδος μᾶλλον . . μίμησις ἢ
				ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.95
			</span></i>; of a naval command, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				6.2.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Athens,
				<i>office of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				192
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.41
			</span></i>: in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				36b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				599c
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς ἐνιαυσίοις
			ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				16
			</span></i>: <i>presidency</i> of the Achaean league, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.37.1
			</span></i>, etc.; in Egypt, <i>office of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός, πρὸς τῇ ς</span>.
				deputy<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-στρατηγός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PEnteux.</u>
				63.10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				108.28
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τῇ
			ς</span>. also,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				12.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; at Rome, <i>praetorship</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cat.Mi.</u>
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sull.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, etc.; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.3
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>period of command, campaign</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				6.2.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>troops commanded by one general, command</i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				266.54
			</span></i> (Pergam., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>generalship</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.1.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				307a
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>piece of strategy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				17.23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>province governed by a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				12.1.4
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				6.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				105
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαλαγγαρχία</span>
			, a force of <i><span class="en">
				4096
			</span></i> men, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				10.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				9.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατιά</span>
			 (which is found in codd. AB), <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ju.</u>
				5.3
			</span></i>.</div>
